==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Formed of a root of {{etyl|bat|fi}} origin + the suffix {{term|-e|lang=fi}}. Compare Lithuanian {{term|dõras||good|lang=lt}}. Karelian {{term|tuoreh|lang=krl}} and Votic {{term|toorõh|lang=vot}} are of equivalent structure; Estonian {{term|toores|lang=et}} utilizes a different suffix.

